    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_005d8e4a",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: meme_image; hasOverallIntent: Harmful; overall-intent-description: The image depicts soldiers in combat gear with rifles, set against a war-torn landscape with helicopters in the background. The overlaid text reads: 'when you find a shooter the same day you plan a bombing, so you team up.' This juxtaposition of military imagery with the text creates a darkly humorous or ironic tone, implying a bizarre or absurd scenario where opposing forces (shooter and bomber) unexpectedly collaborate. The intent is not to target any specific group with hate or abuse, but rather to use a provocative and potentially misleading analogy to comment on real-world events or situations involving violence and conflict. The meme's harmfulness stems from its potential to trivialize or sensationalize serious acts of violence, such as shootings and bombings, by framing them as absurd coincidences or opportunities for collaboration. This can normalize or downplay the gravity of such events, potentially causing emotional distress or misunderstanding among viewers, especially if they are affected by such violence. The meme does not contain explicit hate speech or discriminatory content, but its dark humor and implication of collaboration between violent actors can be seen as harmful due to its potential to desensitize viewers to the seriousness of violence and its consequences.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_aca25e6a"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
